/* Style Colours:

- windowColor
- windowForegroundColor
- paneColor
- logForegroundColor
- logBackgroundColor
- windowBorderColor
- windowInternalBorderColor
- buttonColor
- buttonBorderColor
- metroButtonBorderColor
- buttonTextColor
- pressedButtonColor
- pressedButtonTextColor
- hoverButtonColor
- scrollBarColor
- scrollBarBackgroundColor
- scrollBarHoverColor
- tabColor
- tabTextColor
- tabSelectedColor
- tabSelectedTextColor
- toolTipTextColor
- toolTipBaseColor
- statusBarColor
- statusBarTextColor
- sliderColor
- sliderBackgroundColor
- sliderBorderColor
- menuColor
- menuTextColor
- menuSelectedColor
- menuSelectedTextColor
- selectionForegroundColor
- selectionBackgroundColor
- errorBackgroundColor
- highlightedBackgroundColor (the accent)

Derived tokens (computed in SonicPiTheme::reloadStylesheet from the theme
colours: blends and auto-contrast that plain QSS can't express):

- accentContrastTextColor (auto-contrast text on the accent)
- accentHoverColor        (accent lightened for hover fills)
- accentTintColor         (pane washed 6% toward the accent)
- accentTintStrongColor   (pane washed 14% toward the accent)
- softForegroundColor     (foreground -> pane emphasis ramp: 10%)
- mutedForegroundColor    (30%)
- faintForegroundColor    (62%)
- ghostForegroundColor    (82%)
- subtleFillColor         (pane nudged 7% toward the foreground)
- flashWashColor          (translucent accent wash, rgba)
- focusWashColor          (translucent accent-contrast wash, rgba)

- fixedWidthFont

Corner radius. One scale, three steps, picked by the element's role so that
elements of the same kind always agree (see dpi.h). Already DPI-scaled — use
these rather than a literal, which is how the curvature drifted apart before:

- radiusSmall  (controls: fields, buttons, combos, handles)
- radiusMedium (surfaces: cards, frames, panels, list containers)
- radiusLarge  (segmented navigation: nav chips, selection rows, deck selectors)
- radiusLargeOuter (a container wrapping those rows — see "concentric" in dpi.h:
                    a parent must curve wider than its child, never tighter)

Note about auto scaling
-----------------------

All dx values are autoscaled for the resolution of the screen. 0 will always return 0, values greater than 0 will always return at least 1.

Values 1->25 will be scaled in integer increments. Values 30 - 100 will be rounded down to the nearest 10 and scaled. Values 100 -> 500 will be rounded down to the nearest 100 and scaled.

*/

*
{
  /* `transparent`, not `none`: none is only valid for the `background`
     shorthand — as a background-color brush it is undefined, and some Qt
     builds (Linux distro Qt) paint it black instead of ignoring it. */
  background-color: transparent;
  color:  windowForegroundColor;
}

*#prefs
{
   background: windowColor;
   border: 8dx solid scrollBarHoverColor;

}

*#prefs:hover
{
   border: 8dx solid tabSelectedColor;

}


*#scopes
{
    background: paneColor;
}

QWidget#mainWidget
{
  background: paneColor;
}

QSplitter
{
    background: paneColor;
}


/* Splitter handles are custom-painted by ThinSplitterHandle (thinsplitter.h).
   Don't add a QSplitter::handle rule here — it routes them through Qt's
   stylesheet style and clobbers the thin-line paint and hover reveal. */

QFrame
{
  border: none;
}

QLabel
{
  border: none;
}


QTabBar
{

}

QTabBar::tab
{

    background: tabColor;
    color: tabTextColor;
    /* padding shrunk by the border width so tab geometry is unchanged */
    border: 2dx solid transparent;
    padding-top: 3dx;
    padding-right: 8dx;
    padding-bottom: 3dx;
    padding-left: 8dx;
}

QTabBar::tab:focus
{
    border: 2dx solid hoverButtonColor;
}

QTabBar::tab:hover {
    background: scrollBarHoverColor;
    color: scrollBarHoverTextColor;
}

QTabBar::tab:selected
{
    background: tabSelectedColor;
    color: tabSelectedTextColor;

}

QTabBar::tab:hover:selected
{
    background: tabSelectedColor;
    color: tabSelectedTextColor;

}

/* Cards / Docs / Logs / Debug side tabs are icon-only: size each tab snugly
   around its (uniform) icon so the glyph is centred by construction — Qt
   start-aligns icons along the tab axis, so any spare length reads as
   misalignment. The child combinator (>) limits this to southTabs' own bar
   so the nested Docs sub-tabs (Tutorial / Examples / Synths …) are left
   alone. */
QTabWidget#southTabs > QTabBar::tab
{
    /* Size comes from IconTabBar::tabSizeHint (square); no padding here so
       it doesn't transpose awkwardly on the vertical bar. */
    padding: 0dx;
}

QTabWidget
{
    background: paneColor;
}

QTabWidget::tab-bar
{
    alignment: center;

}

QTabWidget::pane
{
    border: 0dx;

}

/* South dock: pages sit flush against the icon tab bar (the Cards pane's
   page-back zone reaches all the way to the tabs). */
QTabWidget#southTabs::pane
{
    border: 0dx;
    margin: 0dx;
    padding: 0dx;
}

QDockWidget::title
{
    /* Match the SuperSonic debug pane's log titles: 11px Hack, muted, left. */
    color: paneTitleColor;
    border: 0dx;
    text-align: left;
    background: logBackgroundColor;
    font-family: 'Hack';
    font-size: paneTitleFontPx;
    padding-left: 6dx;
}

QDockWidget
{
  /* Opaque themed frame so a floated-out pane isn't a bare white window. */
  background: paneColor;
}

/* Shared "section title" look, matching the SuperSonic debug pane's log titles
   (DEBUG / TO SUPERSONIC / FROM SUPERSONIC): small, muted, left-aligned Hack.
   Text is uppercased by the code that creates the label. */
QLabel#paneTitle
{
    font-family: 'Hack';
    font-weight: normal;
    color: paneTitleColor;
    background: logBackgroundColor;
    padding: 3dx 6dx 3dx 6dx;
}

/* Dock title row that hosts controls beside the title (Scope, Help). Same
   background as the #paneTitle chip so the label and row read as one strip. */
QWidget#dockTitleBar
{
    background: logBackgroundColor;
}

/* Per-control section labels inside the Link widget — subordinate to the
   widget title: smaller, no background chip, so they don't compete with it. */
QLabel#linkSectionLabel
{
    font-family: 'Hack';
    font-weight: normal;
    color: paneTitleColor;
}

/* Fallback only: app tooltips are drawn by SonicPiToolTip (an anchored,
   caret-pointing popup — see widgets/sonicpitooltip.h). This styles any
   stock QToolTip that slips through (e.g. from third-party widgets). */
 QToolTip
 {
    color: toolTipTextColor;
    background-color: toolTipBaseColor;
    border: 1dx solid toolTipTextColor;
    padding: 4dx;
}

QSlider
{
    width: 35dx;
}


QSlider::groove:vertical
{
    margin: 2dx;
    background: sliderBackgroundColor;
    border-radius: radiusSmall;
    border: 2dx solid sliderBorderColor;
}

QSlider::handle:vertical
{
    border: 1dx solid black;
    border-radius: radiusSmall;
    height: 30dx;
    background-color: sliderColor;
}

QSlider::handle:vertical:hover
{
    background-color: scrollBarHoverColor;
}

QSlider::handle:vertical:focus
{
    background-color: hoverButtonColor;
}

QMenu
{
    background: menuColor;
    color: menuTextColor;
}

QMenu:selected
{
    background: menuSelectedColor;
    color: menuSelectedTextColor;
}


QMenuBar {
    background: menuBarColor;
}

QMenuBar::item {
    background: menuColor;
    color: menuTextColor;
}

QMenuBar::item:selected {
    background: menuSelectedColor;
    color: menuSelectedTextColor;
}

/* Dock separators are custom-painted by DividerProxyStyle (dividerproxystyle.h).
   Don't add a QMainWindow::separator rule here — it routes them through Qt's
   stylesheet style and clobbers the thin-line paint and hover reveal. */

QMainWindow
{
    background-color: transparent;
    color: windowColor;
}

QwtPlot
{
    background-color: paneColor;
}

QwtPlotGLCanvas
{
    background-color: paneColor;
}

QStatusBar
{
    background-color: statusBarColor;
    color: statusBarTextColor;
}

QStatusBar::item{
    border: none;
}

QPlainTextEdit
{
    background-color: logBackgroundColor;
    color: logForegroundColor;
    border: 0dx;
}


QCheckBox {
    spacing: 15dx;
    border: 2dx solid transparent;
}

/* Focus ring only for KEYBOARD focus (kbFocus property, set by SettingsWidget's
   app-wide event filter) — a mouse click toggles without drawing a box around
   the row. */
QCheckBox[kbFocus="true"]
{
    border: 2dx solid hoverButtonColor;
}

QCheckBox::indicator {
    width: 18dx;
    height: 18dx;
}

QCheckBox::hover:!pressed
{

    color: hoverButtonColor;
}

QCheckBox::indicator:unchecked {
    image: url(:/images/checkbox-unchecked.png);
}

QCheckBox::indicator:checked {
    image: url("checkboxCheckedImage");
}


QRadioButton
{
    color: windowForegroundColor;
    background: windowColor;
    border: 2dx solid transparent;
}

QRadioButton:focus
{
    border: 2dx solid hoverButtonColor;
}

QGroupBox QFrame
{
    background: windowColor;
}

QGroupBox
{


  /* Extra top padding: breathing room between the section header and the
     first control. */
  padding-top: 12dx;
    padding-right: 10dx;
    padding-bottom: 5dx;
    padding-left: 10dx;


    subcontrol-origin: margin;
    margin-top: 15dx;
    margin-bottom: 15dx;
    font-weight: italic;
    background-color: windowColor;
    border: 1dx solid windowInternalBorderColor;
}

QDockWidget QListView
{
    color: windowForegroundColor;
    selection-color: selectionForegroundColor;
    selection-background-color: selectionBackgroundColor;
    outline: 10dx;

}

QTextBrowser
{
    selection-color: selectionForegroundColor;
    selection-background-color: selectionBackgroundColor;
    /* No scroll-area padding: it would inset the scrollbar and break the
       shared 2dx offset. The 20dx text inset is applied via documentMargin
       (see setDocumentMargin calls) so the bar stays flush to the edge. */
    background-color: paneColor;
}

QListWidget
{
    border: 1dx solid windowBorderColor;
    background: paneColor;
    min-width: 500dx;
}

QListWidget:focus
{
    border: 1dx solid hoverButtonColor;
}

QListWidget::item
{
    background: paneColor;
    color: menuTextColor;
}

/* Hover highlight so the help nav list responds to the pointer like the docs do,
   with auto-contrasting text on the hover fill. */
QListWidget::item:hover
{
    background: scrollBarHoverColor;
    color: scrollBarHoverTextColor;
}

QListWidget::item::selected
{
    background: menuSelectedColor;
    color: menuSelectedTextColor;
}

/* ── Docs panel navigation ───────────────────────────────────────────────
   The help nav is a filter field over a chapter list, with chip-style tabs
   below (Tutorial / Examples / …). Everything stays a stock Qt widget —
   QLineEdit / QListWidget / QTabBar — so screen readers keep their native
   roles; only the chrome changes: no sunken frames, pill selection rows,
   and a keyboard focus ring that never collides with the resting look
   (transparent resting borders keep geometry stable). */

/* The nav column is a tinted sidebar — its own surface against the content
   pane, like the nav rail of a docs site. */
QWidget#docsNavPage
{
    background: windowColor;
}

/* Chapter list: borderless and padded, with full-width rounded selection rows.
   The selected row (auto-contrast text on the accent) doubles as the focus
   landmark; the rounded ring below appears when the list itself has focus. */
QListWidget#docsNavList
{
    border: 2dx solid transparent;
    /* Concentric with the rows inside it: the focus ring has to curve wider
       than the rows it wraps, or their corners cut across it. Keep this
       padding at kNavRowInsetDx — the token is derived from it. */
    border-radius: radiusLargeOuter;
    background: transparent;
    padding: 4dx;
    min-width: 200dx;
}

QListWidget#docsNavList:focus
{
    border: 2dx solid hoverButtonColor;
}

QListWidget#docsNavList::item
{
    background: transparent;
    color: windowForegroundColor;
    border-radius: radiusLarge;
    padding-top: 4dx;
    padding-bottom: 4dx;
    padding-left: 9dx;
    padding-right: 9dx;
}

QListWidget#docsNavList::item:hover
{
    background: scrollBarHoverColor;
    color: scrollBarHoverTextColor;
}

QListWidget#docsNavList::item:selected
{
    background: menuSelectedColor;
    color: menuSelectedTextColor;
}

/* Filter field: a pill-shaped search box with a quiet outline that swaps to
   the focus accent at the same 2dx weight (no layout shift on focus). */
/* Quiet at rest (just the magnifier + placeholder on the column tint);
   the field chrome appears on hover and fills on focus. */
QLineEdit#docsFilter
{
    background: transparent;
    color: windowForegroundColor;
    border: 2dx solid transparent;
    border-radius: radiusLarge;
    min-height: 20dx;
    padding-top: 2dx;
    padding-bottom: 2dx;
    padding-left: 8dx;
    padding-right: 8dx;
}

QLineEdit#docsFilter:hover
{
    border: 2dx solid faintForegroundColor;
}

QLineEdit#docsFilter:focus
{
    background: paneColor;
    border: 2dx solid hoverButtonColor;
}

/* Docs sub-tabs (Tutorial / Examples / Synths / …) and the Info window's
   tabs: rounded chips in the house segmented-control style instead of boxy
   legacy tabs. Selected chip fills with the accent (auto-contrast text);
   keyboard focus keeps the standard 2dx ring, which integrates with the
   chip radius. */
QTabWidget#docsNavTabs::pane,
QTabWidget#infoNavTabs::pane
{
    border: none;
}

/* One surface for the whole nav column: the chip strip sits on the same tint
   as the pages below it (#docsNavPage), so it reads as the column's header
   rather than a floating row of words. */
QTabWidget#docsNavTabs
{
    background: windowColor;
}

/* ── House style: "chip" ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Outlined chip at rest, hover-accent border on hover, solid selected fill
   (no border) when current. Used by the docs/info nav chips here and the
   Cards deck selector (#qsDeckPill below): one grammar, two sizes. Softened
   corners, deliberately short of a capsule — see the scale in dpi.h. */
QTabWidget#docsNavTabs > QTabBar::tab,
QTabWidget#infoNavTabs > QTabBar::tab
{
    background: transparent;
    color: windowForegroundColor;
    border: 2dx solid faintForegroundColor;
    border-radius: radiusLarge;
    font-weight: 600;
    padding-top: 3dx;
    padding-bottom: 3dx;
    padding-left: 9dx;
    padding-right: 9dx;
    margin-top: 2dx;
    margin-bottom: 3dx;
    margin-left: 1dx;
    margin-right: 1dx;
}

QTabWidget#docsNavTabs > QTabBar::tab:hover,
QTabWidget#infoNavTabs > QTabBar::tab:hover
{
    border-color: hoverButtonColor;
}

QTabWidget#docsNavTabs > QTabBar::tab:selected,
QTabWidget#infoNavTabs > QTabBar::tab:selected
{
    background: tabSelectedColor;
    color: tabSelectedTextColor;
    border-color: transparent;
}

QTabWidget#docsNavTabs > QTabBar::tab:focus,
QTabWidget#infoNavTabs > QTabBar::tab:focus
{
    border: 2dx solid hoverButtonColor;
}

/* ── Info window ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   A top-level tool window, so it carries its own chrome: the window surface
   is the frame, and the page sits on it as a card. The card takes its form
   from the fill contrast against that frame — no outline, which at 1dx only
   reads as a seam. Radius matches the docs example frames. */
QWidget#infoWindow
{
    background: windowColor;
}

QTextBrowser#infoPage
{
    background: paneColor;
    border: none;
    border-radius: radiusMedium;
}

/* Primary navigation for the window, so the chips are roomier than the docs
   sub-nav they share a grammar with — but only in padding. The radius stays
   on the shared pill step, so these read as the same control as the Help
   pane's chips rather than a second, nearly-identical curve. */
QTabWidget#infoNavTabs > QTabBar::tab
{
    padding-top: 6dx;
    padding-bottom: 6dx;
    padding-left: 16dx;
    padding-right: 16dx;
    margin-top: 12dx;
    margin-bottom: 2dx;
    margin-left: 3dx;
    margin-right: 3dx;
}

QComboBox
{
    /* No resting border (transparent keeps geometry stable against the 1dx
       hover/focus borders below). */
    border: 1dx solid transparent;
    border-radius: radiusSmall;
    /* min-height (not padding) gives the box its height — padding would push
       the text into a fixed content area and clip the glyphs. Row gaps come
       from the grid's vertical spacing, not from the combo. */
    min-height: 22dx;
    padding-top: 1dx;
    padding-right: 18dx;
    padding-bottom: 1dx;
    padding-left: 6dx;
    background: tabColor;
    color: tabTextColor;
}

QComboBox::item
{
    background: tabColor;
    color: tabTextColor;
    selection-color: tabSelectedTextColor;
    selection-background-color: tabSelectedColor;
}

QComboBox:hover
{
    border-radius: radiusSmall;
    border-color: hoverButtonColor;
    background: hoverButtonColor;
}

QComboBox:focus
{
    border: 1dx solid hoverButtonColor;
}

QComboBox::item::selected
{
    background: tabSelectedColor;
    color: tabSelectedTextColor;
}

QComboBox:on
{ /* shift the text when the popup opens */
    color: buttonTextColor;
}

QComboBox::drop-down
{
    border-style: none;
}


QToolBar
{
    background-color: windowColor;
    border-bottom: 0dx;

}

QToolButton
{
    padding: 4dx;
    padding-right: 5dx;
    margin-top: 6dx;
    margin-bottom: 6dx;
    background-color: transparent;
    border-radius: 0dx;
    border-bottom: 2px solid transparent;
    border-top: 2px solid transparent;
}

QToolButton::hover
{
    border-bottom: 2px solid scrollBarHoverColor;
    border-top: 2px solid scrollBarHoverColor;
}

QToolButton::hover::pressed
{
    border-bottom: 2px solid tabSelectedColor;
    border-top: 2px solid tabSelectedColor;
}

QToolButton:focus
{
    border-bottom: 2px solid hoverButtonColor;
    border-top: 2px solid hoverButtonColor;
}

/* Dock-title-row icon buttons: the help pane's persistent close ✕ and the
   A-/A+ zoom pairs (zoombar.cpp). Flat: the glyphs carry their own form, so
   the buttons draw no chip; hover brightens the glyph in code. One shared
   rule so all their boxes are identical and the row's icons space evenly. */
QPushButton#helpCloseButton,
QPushButton#zoomBtn
{
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
    border-radius: radiusSmall;
    padding: 2px;
}

QGroupBox:title
{
    subcontrol-origin: margin;
    top: 0dx;
    padding-top: 10dx;
    padding-right: 10dx;
    padding-bottom: 20dx;
    padding-left: 5dx;
    color: windowForegroundColor;
    background-color: windowColor;
}

/* Scrollbars — unified across both axes and every pane. A 10dx strip
   carries an 8dx fully-rounded capsule handle that sits a constant 2dx off
   the trailing edge (right for vertical, bottom for horizontal). The 2dx
   gap lives on the handle, not the container, so the offset is identical
   everywhere regardless of each pane's own border/padding. No arrow
   buttons; the handle runs the full length of the track. Vertical and
   horizontal are exact mirrors of each other.
   NB: keep panes free of scroll-area padding (it would shove the whole
   strip inward and break the shared offset — pad text via documentMargin
   instead). */

QScrollBar:vertical,
QScrollBar:horizontal
{
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
    margin: 0px;
}

QScrollBar:vertical
{
    width: 10dx;
}

QScrollBar:horizontal
{
    height: 10dx;
}

QScrollBar::handle:vertical,
QScrollBar::handle:horizontal
{
    background: scrollBarColor;
    border-radius: radiusSmall;
}

/* 2dx capsule inset off the trailing edge (right for vertical, bottom for
   horizontal). MUST be single-value longhand margins: the dx→px preprocessor
   (ScalePxInStyleSheet) only rewrites a dx token that comes straight after a
   colon, so a shorthand like `margin: 0dx 2dx 0dx 0dx` leaves the later
   values un-scaled and Qt drops the whole declaration. Zeros are literal 0px
   for the same reason (there is no 0dx rule in the preprocessor). */
QScrollBar::handle:vertical
{
    min-height: 24dx;
    margin-left: 0px;
    margin-right: 2dx;
}

QScrollBar::handle:horizontal
{
    min-width: 24dx;
    margin-top: 0px;
    margin-bottom: 2dx;
}

QScrollBar::handle:hover
{
    background: scrollBarHoverColor;
}

/* No arrow buttons. */
QScrollBar::add-line:vertical,
QScrollBar::sub-line:vertical,
QScrollBar::add-line:horizontal,
QScrollBar::sub-line:horizontal
{
    width: 0px;
    height: 0px;
    background: none;
    border: none;
}

/* Empty track stays transparent. */
QScrollBar::add-page:vertical,
QScrollBar::sub-page:vertical,
QScrollBar::add-page:horizontal,
QScrollBar::sub-page:horizontal
{
    background: none;
}

QPushButton
{
    /* Buttons are black in every theme by design; the border (white in dark,
       light-grey in light) gives them their form, the text stays white. Routed
       through a token (not literal black) so it still inverts / greys with the
       global colour toggles. */
    background-color: buttonBackgroundColor;
    color: buttonTextColor;
    padding: 5dx;
    border-radius: radiusSmall;
    border: 2dx solid buttonBorderColor;
    height: 25dx;
}

QPushButton::pressed
{
    background-color: pressedButtonColor;
    color: pressedButtonTextColor;
}

QPushButton::hover:!pressed
{
    background-color: hoverButtonColor;
    color: hoverButtonTextColor;
}

QPushButton:focus
{
    border: 2dx solid hoverButtonColor;
}

QMessageBox
{
    background: windowColor;
}

/* ── House style: "segmented control" ────────────────────────────────────
   A pill of mutually-exclusive buttons (recording format, shortcut scheme, …).
   One shared rule via the `segmented` property, so every picker matches —
   instead of each widget carrying its own inline stylesheet. */
QWidget[segmented="true"]
{
    background: rgba(127,127,127,70);
    border-radius: radiusMedium;
}

/* QToolButton included: the recording picker uses tool buttons so a large
   icon can sit above the label (TextUnderIcon). */
QWidget[segmented="true"] QPushButton,
QWidget[segmented="true"] QToolButton
{
    border: none;
    padding: 6px 16px;
    border-radius: radiusSmall;
    background: transparent;
    color: palette(window-text);
    /* QToolButton isn't covered by the app-wide QPushButton font rule, so
       pin the size here to keep segment labels on the house scale. */
}

QWidget[segmented="true"] QPushButton:hover:!checked,
QWidget[segmented="true"] QToolButton:hover:!checked
{
    background: rgba(127,127,127,70);
}

QWidget[segmented="true"] QPushButton:checked,
QWidget[segmented="true"] QToolButton:checked
{
    background: palette(highlight);
    color: palette(highlighted-text);
}


QPushButton#enableLinkButton
{
  min-width: 100dx;
}

/* Metro-row buttons: theme-dependent resting border — transparent on light
   panes (no grey ring), white on dark panes where the black pill needs it
   for form. Active/flashing states set their own borders. */
QPushButton#enableLinkButton,
QPushButton#tapButton,
QPushButton#linkStreamsButton
{
  border: 2dx solid metroButtonBorderColor;
}

/* These ID rules outrank the generic focus ring, so keyboard focus is
   re-asserted here (same pattern as #rowVisibility below). */
QPushButton#enableLinkButton:focus,
QPushButton#tapButton:focus,
QPushButton#linkStreamsButton:focus
{
  border: 2dx solid hoverButtonColor;
}

/* ── House style: "active pill" ──────────────────────────────────────────
   Shared selected/on look: highlight fill with a border matching that fill
   (seamless, stable 2dx). Used by the Link button, the streams chevron and
   the share-audio toggle. (The muted share-audio :checked below overrides
   this with a dimmed fill via its more specific selector.) */
QPushButton#enableLinkButton[linkOn="true"],
QPushButton#enableLinkButton[linkOn="true"]:hover,
QPushButton#linkStreamsButton:checked,
QPushButton#linkStreamsButton:checked:hover,
QPushButton#shareAudioToggle:checked,
QPushButton#shareAudioToggle:checked:hover
{
  background-color: selectionBackgroundColor;
  color: selectionForegroundColor;
  border: 2dx solid selectionBackgroundColor;
}

QPushButton#tapTempo
{
  min-width: 100dx;
}

/* Brief tap flash — driven by the flashing dynamic property so we
   don't have to swap stylesheets on/off in C++. */
QPushButton#tapButton[flashing="true"]
{
  background-color: pressedButtonColor;
  color: pressedButtonTextColor;
  border-color: paneColor;
}

/* Streams-panel expand / collapse chevron. Its :checked "active" look is the
   shared "active pill" rule above (highlight fill, seamless border). */
QPushButton#linkStreamsButton
{
  min-width: 28dx;
}

/* Network-visibility button: a bare glyph — no fill, no border (2dx transparent
   keeps it the same size as the other buttons). The glyph colour carries the
   state (pink when Link is on, white when off; set in code). Hover only. */
QPushButton#rowVisibility
{
  min-width: 28dx;
  background: transparent;
  border: 2dx solid transparent;
}

QPushButton#rowVisibility:hover
{
  background-color: hoverButtonColor;
}

/* This ID rule's transparent border outranks the generic focus ring, so
   keyboard focus is re-asserted here. */
QPushButton#rowVisibility:focus
{
  border-color: hoverButtonColor;
}
QLineEdit
{
    border-radius: radiusSmall;
    border: 2dx solid transparent;
}

QLineEdit:focus
{
    border: 2dx solid hoverButtonColor;
}

/* BPM scrubber. The resting (link-off) look lives here; the `linkOn` and `cue`
   dynamic properties drive the link-engaged border and the transient
   change/reset edit cues — replacing the old per-edit inline full-stylesheet
   rebuilds. */
QLineEdit#bpmScrubber
{
    selection-color: selectionForegroundColor;
    selection-background-color: selectionBackgroundColor;
    color: highlightedBackgroundColor;
    background-color: paneColor;
    border: 2dx solid highlightedBackgroundColor;
    padding: 5dx;
    min-width: 105dx;
    max-width: 125dx;
    height: 25dx;

}

/* Link engaged: border tracks the pressed/active colour. */
QLineEdit#bpmScrubber[linkOn="true"]
{
    border: 2dx solid pressedButtonColor;
}

QLineEdit#bpmScrubber::hover:!pressed,
QLineEdit#bpmScrubber::hover:pressed
{
    background-color: hoverButtonColor;
    color: hoverButtonTextColor;
}

QLineEdit#bpmScrubber[linkOn="true"]::hover:!pressed,
QLineEdit#bpmScrubber[linkOn="true"]::hover:pressed
{
    background-color: pressedButtonColor;
    color: pressedButtonTextColor;
}

/* Placed after the linkOn rule (equal specificity) so keyboard focus stays
   visible whether or not Link is engaged; the cue flashes below still win. */
QLineEdit#bpmScrubber:focus
{
    border: 2dx solid windowForegroundColor;
}

/* Transient edit cues — C++ sets cue=change/reset then clears to "none" after
   250ms. change = pressed fill; reset = inverted flash. */
QLineEdit#bpmScrubber[cue="change"]
{
    color: pressedButtonTextColor;
    border-color: pressedButtonColor;
    background-color: pressedButtonColor;
}

QLineEdit#bpmScrubber[cue="reset"]
{
    color: paneColor;
    border-color: buttonTextColor;
    background-color: windowForegroundColor;
}


QLineEdit#timeWarpEdit
{
    selection-color: selectionForegroundColor;
    selection-background-color: selectionBackgroundColor;
    color: highlightedBackgroundColor;
    background-color: paneColor;
    border: 2dx solid highlightedBackgroundColor;
    padding: 5dx;
    max-width: 80dx;
    height: 25dx;

}

QLineEdit#timeWarpEdit:focus
{
    border: 2dx solid hoverButtonColor;
}

QLineEdit#timeWarpEdit::hover:!pressed
{
    background-color: hoverButtonColor;
    color: hoverButtonTextColor;
}

QLineEdit#timeWarpEdit::hover:pressed
{
    background-color: hoverButtonColor;
    color: hoverButtonTextColor;
}

/* Transient warp-applied flash — driven by the `flashing` dynamic property
   (C++ toggles it + repolishes, then clears after 250ms), replacing the old
   inline full-stylesheet rebuild. */
QLineEdit#timeWarpEdit[flashing="true"]
{
    color: pressedButtonTextColor;
    border-color: pressedButtonColor;
    background-color: pressedButtonColor;
}

SonicPiMetro
{
    background-color: windowColor;
}

/* Muted helper/footnote labels — house small size + the theme's placeholder
   (dimmed-but-legible) foreground, replacing hardcoded 10px / "gray" inline. */
QLabel#asioInputNote,
QLabel#remoteSessionNote,
QLabel#poweredByLabel
{
    color: palette(placeholder-text);
}

QLabel#asioInputNote
{
    margin-left: 18dx;
}


/* ── Link Audio Streams panel (inline in the metro pane) ── */

LinkAudioStreamsWidget QLabel,
LinkAudioStreamsWidget QCheckBox,
LinkAudioStreamsWidget QLineEdit
{
}

QLineEdit#linkPeerName
{
    background-color: paneColor;
    color: windowForegroundColor;
    /* Match the Global Time Warp field: a soft grey (Button), not the harsh
       white of ButtonBorder. */
    border: 2dx solid buttonColor;
    border-radius: radiusSmall;
    /* Match the Global Time Warp field's text padding (uniform 5dx). */
    padding: 5dx;
    selection-color: selectionForegroundColor;
    selection-background-color: selectionBackgroundColor;
}

/* Link Name border goes pink while Link is engaged. */
QLineEdit#linkPeerName[linkOn="true"]
{
    border: 2dx solid selectionBackgroundColor;
}

/* After the linkOn rule (equal specificity) so the keyboard focus ring
   stays visible while Link is engaged. */
QLineEdit#linkPeerName:focus
{
    border: 2dx solid hoverButtonColor;
}

/* Share-audio: a checkable pill button. Same border / radius / height
   as Link / Tap / BPM / TimeWarp (inherited from the base QPushButton
   rule), with a light "off" fill matching BPM / TimeWarp — these are
   value-selectors, not action buttons, so the unfilled look matches
   their semantic family. Active state fills with the pink highlight. */
QPushButton#shareAudioToggle
{
    background-color: paneColor;
    color: windowForegroundColor;
    min-width: 70dx;
}

QPushButton#shareAudioToggle:hover
{
    background-color: hoverButtonColor;
    color: buttonTextColor;
}

/* #shareAudioToggle:checked "active" look is the shared "active pill" rule
   near the top of the button section (highlight fill, seamless border). */

/* "Muted" state (Link is off — setting has no effect right now).
   Still fully clickable so users can discover it's a button. Dimmed but
   legible: palette(mid) is near-invisible dark-grey-on-black, so use the
   placeholder-text role, which is derived to stay readable at reduced
   emphasis across light/dark/high-contrast themes. The checked variant
   still uses palette(mid) as a fill, where contrast isn't an issue. */
QPushButton#shareAudioToggle[muted="true"],
QPushButton#shareAudioToggle[muted="true"]:hover
{
    color: palette(placeholder-text);
}

QPushButton#shareAudioToggle[muted="true"]:checked,
QPushButton#shareAudioToggle[muted="true"]:checked:hover
{
    /* buttonTextColor (white) — Mid is a dark fill in every theme, so
       white stays legible everywhere; placeholder-text sank into the
       light theme's grey Mid. */
    color: buttonTextColor;
    background-color: palette(mid);
    border: 2dx solid palette(mid);
}

/* Link Audio latency slider — without explicit groove/handle styling
   the native macOS slider renders as a zero-height track that's
   effectively invisible inside our compact panel row. Mirrors the
   timeWarpSlider pattern in the metro row. */
QSlider#linkLatencySlider
{
    min-height: 20dx;
}

/* Match the Global Time Warp slider so the two sliders are consistent. */
QSlider#linkLatencySlider::groove:horizontal
{
    height: 4dx;
    background: windowBorderColor;
    margin: 2dx 0;
}

QSlider#linkLatencySlider::handle:horizontal
{
    background: buttonColor;
    width: 18dx;
    height: 25dx;
    margin: -5px 0;
    border-radius: radiusSmall;
}

QSlider#linkLatencySlider::handle:horizontal:hover
{
    background: hoverButtonColor;
}

QSlider#linkLatencySlider::handle:horizontal:focus
{
    background: hoverButtonColor;
}

QLabel#linkLatencyValue
{
    color: windowForegroundColor;
}


/* Table doubles as a Link-state indicator via its borders — grey when
   Link is off (same palette(mid) used by the muted Visibility thumb),
   pink when Link is on (same selectionBackgroundColor as the active
   thumb). Header and rows share a small font so the whole card reads
   as one tight unit; only the header is bold. */
QTableWidget#linkPeersTable
{
    background-color: paneColor;
    color: windowForegroundColor;
    border: 1dx solid palette(mid);
    border-radius: radiusMedium;
    gridline-color: paneColor;
    alternate-background-color: windowColor;
    selection-background-color: selectionBackgroundColor;
    selection-color: selectionForegroundColor;
}

QTableWidget#linkPeersTable[linkOn="true"]
{
    border: 1dx solid selectionBackgroundColor;
}

QTableWidget#linkPeersTable QHeaderView
{
    background-color: paneColor;
    border-bottom: 1dx solid palette(mid);
}

QTableWidget#linkPeersTable[linkOn="true"] QHeaderView
{
    border-bottom: 1dx solid selectionBackgroundColor;
}

QTableWidget#linkPeersTable QHeaderView::section
{
    background-color: paneColor;
    color: windowForegroundColor;
    border: none;
    padding: 3dx 8dx;
    font-size: smallFontPx;
    font-weight: bold;
}

QTableWidget#linkPeersTable::item
{
    padding: 1dx 8dx;
}

QSlider#timeWarpSlider
{
min-height: 20dx;
min-width: 80dx;
}

QSlider#timeWarpSlider::groove:horizontal {
    height: 4dx; /* the groove expands to the size of the slider by default. by giving it a height, it has a fixed size */
    background: windowBorderColor;
    margin: 2dx 0;

}

QSlider#timeWarpSlider::handle:horizontal {
    background: highlightedBackgroundColor;
    width: 18dx;
    height: 25dx;
    margin: -5px 0; /* handle is placed by default on the contents rect of the groove. Expand outside the groove */

    border-radius: radiusSmall;
}

QSlider#timeWarpSlider::handle:horizontal:hover {
    background: hoverButtonColor;
}

QSlider#timeWarpSlider::handle:horizontal:focus {
    background: hoverButtonColor;
}

/* ── Quickstart Cards pane ──────────────────────────────────────────────
   Font sizes track the pane's own zoom, so they're set per-widget in
   quickstartpane.cpp; everything theme-coloured lives here. */

QuickstartPane
{
    background-color: paneColor;
}

QuickstartPane QScrollArea
{
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
}

/* Deck selector: the house pill grammar (see #docsNavTabs above), sized up
   for the deck bar. `current` marks the active deck. */
QPushButton#qsDeckPill
{
    background-color: transparent;
    color: windowForegroundColor;
    border: 2dx solid faintForegroundColor;
    border-radius: radiusLarge;
    padding-top: 6dx;
    padding-bottom: 6dx;
    padding-left: 14dx;
    padding-right: 14dx;
    font-weight: 600;
}

QPushButton#qsDeckPill:hover
{
    border-color: hoverButtonColor;
}

QPushButton#qsDeckPill:focus
{
    border-color: hoverButtonColor;
}

QPushButton#qsDeckPill[current="true"]
{
    background-color: tabSelectedColor;
    color: tabSelectedTextColor;
    border-color: transparent;
}

/* Carousel nav: ‹ dots › grouped in a soft pill. */
/* Radius set in code alongside the row's scaled height — see qsDot above. */
QWidget#qsNav
{
    background: subtleFillColor;
}

QPushButton#qsArrow
{
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
    color: mutedForegroundColor;
    font-weight: 700;
}

QPushButton#qsArrow:hover:enabled
{
    color: highlightedBackgroundColor;
}

QPushButton#qsArrow:disabled
{
    color: ghostForegroundColor;
}

/* One dot per card; the lit run is the cards currently on screen. */
/* Radius is set per-dot in quickstartpane.cpp (rebuildDots): it must be half
   the dot's size, and the size scales with the pane's A-/A+ zoom. A fixed
   radius here would snap the dot from circle to square as it grew. */
QPushButton#qsDot
{
    border: none;
    padding: 0;
    background: faintForegroundColor;
}

QPushButton#qsDot:hover
{
    background: mutedForegroundColor;
}

QPushButton#qsDot[lit="true"],
QPushButton#qsDot[lit="true"]:hover
{
    background: highlightedBackgroundColor;
}

/* Deck description row: accent rail + muted one-liner. */
/* Radius set in code alongside the rail's scaled width — see qsDot above. */
QWidget#qsHeaderRail
{
    background: highlightedBackgroundColor;
}

QLabel#qsDeckDesc
{
    color: softForegroundColor;
    background: transparent;
}

/* The card. A 2dx border is always reserved (transparent when idle) so the
   hover highlight causes no layout shift; the outer radius = child radius +
   border width so it hugs the rounded header/footer corners. The #qsCard ID
   keeps the border off QLabel children (QLabel derives from QFrame). */
QFrame#qsCard
{
    background: transparent;
    border: 2dx solid transparent;
    border-radius: radiusMedium;
}

/* The selected card: arrow keys move the selection one card at a time and
   the deck scrolls to keep it in view. */
QFrame#qsCard:focus
{
    border-color: windowForegroundColor;
}

QWidget#qsCardHeader
{
    background-color: highlightedBackgroundColor;
    border-top-left-radius: 6dx;
    border-top-right-radius: 6dx;
}

QLabel#qsCardTitle
{
    color: accentContrastTextColor;
    background: transparent;
    font-weight: 700;
}

/* Header icon buttons (copy / add / drag): bare glyphs on the accent bar.
   Hover fills with the code-body tint (the glyph swap to matching ink is done
   in code); the :focus wash is for keyboard users. corner="tr" rounds the
   drag handle's outer corner to match the card. */
QPushButton#qsCardBtn
{
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 0;
    padding: 0;
    outline: none;
}

QPushButton#qsCardBtn:focus
{
    background: focusWashColor;
}

QPushButton#qsCardBtn:hover
{
    background: accentTintColor;
}

QPushButton#qsCardBtn[corner="tr"]
{
    border-top-right-radius: 6dx;
}

QWidget#qsCardBody
{
    background-color: accentTintColor;
}

QLabel#qsCodeLine
{
    color: windowForegroundColor;
    background: transparent;
    font-family: 'Hack';
    border-radius: radiusSmall;
}

/* Trigger flash: the same accent wash the editor uses. */
QLabel#qsCodeLine[flashing="true"]
{
    background: flashWashColor;
}

QWidget#qsCardFooter
{
    background-color: accentTintStrongColor;
    border-bottom-left-radius: 6dx;
    border-bottom-right-radius: 6dx;
}

QLabel#qsCardBlurb
{
    color: softForegroundColor;
    background: transparent;
    font-style: italic;
}

/* The scope is the play/stop control; the disc icon carries the visuals. */
QPushButton#qsCardRun
{
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
}

/* Prefs panel close button. */
QPushButton#prefsHideButton
{
    padding: 5px 18px;
}

/* Covers the corner where the editor's scrollbars meet, which the style
   otherwise paints window-grey against the transparent tracks. */
QWidget#editorScrollCorner
{
    background: paneColor;
}

/* ── Themed confirm dialog (confirmAction in mainwindow.cpp) ── */

QDialog#confirmDialog
{
    background: windowColor;
}

QDialog#confirmDialog QLabel
{
    background: transparent;
    color: windowForegroundColor;
}

QLabel#confirmHeadline
{
    font-weight: bold;
}

QLabel#confirmBody
{
    color: mutedForegroundColor;
}

QDialog#confirmDialog QPushButton
{
    padding: 6px 20px;
    border-radius: radiusSmall;
    border: none;
}

QPushButton#confirmCancel
{
    background: rgba(127,127,127,60);
    color: windowForegroundColor;
}

QPushButton#confirmCancel:hover
{
    background: rgba(127,127,127,110);
}

QPushButton#confirmPrimary
{
    background: highlightedBackgroundColor;
    color: accentContrastTextColor;
}

QPushButton#confirmPrimary:hover
{
    background: accentHoverColor;
}


